From: Seeed Studio <techsupport@seeed.cc>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: rockchip: do not abort set_state on unresolvable pinconf phandle

rockchip_pinctrl_set_state() muxes each pin first, then resolves the pin
config phandle from the 4th cell of rockchip,pins. If it does not resolve,
the loop returns -ENODEV and every remaining pin of the group is left
unmuxed (i2c2m0_xfer = GPIO0_B7/C0: SDA stays GPIO, EEPROM/RTC dead).
pinconf is optional: skip it for that pin and keep muxing the rest.

diff -urN a/drivers/pinctrl/rockchip/pinctrl-rockchip-core.c b/drivers/pinctrl/rockchip/pinctrl-rockchip-core.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/rockchip/pinctrl-rockchip-core.c	2026-09-21 19:38:39.326972318 +0800
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/rockchip/pinctrl-rockchip-core.c	2026-09-21 19:38:39.351725726 +0800
@@ -501,8 +501,11 @@
 			return ret;
 
 		node = ofnode_get_by_phandle(conf);
-		if (!ofnode_valid(node))
-			return -ENODEV;
+		if (!ofnode_valid(node)) {
+			debug("%s: bank %u pin %u: bad conf phandle 0x%x, skip pinconf\n",
+			      __func__, bank, pin, conf);
+			continue;
+		}
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_LIVE)
 		np = ofnode_to_np(node);
 		for (pp = np->properties; pp; pp = pp->next) {
